{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run/draft && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nsub={\\\"action\\\":\\\"review\\\",\n \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Semantic review of the first check for C4-noop-commit-without-bookkeeping (artifact 986da6b1…, executed as the latest C4 run). The item assesses requirement versus predicate, entry and message legality, the oracle and its recover() wrapper, identity correlation, the inference from handler panic to replica termination, and the contrary evidence.\\\",\n \\\"artifact_id\\\":\\\"986da6b1\\\",\n \\\"review_items\\\":[{\n  \\\"aspect\\\":\\\"checker_correspondence\\\",\n  \\\"status\\\":\\\"no_issue_found\\\",\n  \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"S13-handleCommit\\\",\\\"S9-handlePreAccept\\\",\\\"S15-handlePrepareReply\\\"],\n  \\\"report_title\\\":\\\"NOOP 提交使实例所有者空指针崩溃\\\",\n  \\\"report_answer\\\":\\\"由消息创建记录（无 leader bookkeeping）的实例所有者收到一条合法的单 NONE 命令 Commit 后，handleCommit 在重提议分支解引用 inst.lb.clientProposals 触发空指针 panic（事件 panic_value 为 invalid memory address or nil pointer dereference），且该提交未生效（no_effect=true）。运行循环对该处理器没有 recover，因此该 panic 会终止副本进程；这一推断属于限制说明，harness 只观察到 panic 本身。\\\",\n  \\\"rationale\\\":\\\"Requirement versus predicate: the claim is that a legal NOOP commit for an instance the replica owns must be processed without dereferencing absent bookkeeping and without terminating the replica; the predicate asserts panicked == false on the commit-result event, and the retained run reports panicked true with the panic value, plus no_effect true, so the assertion is evaluated on printed fields rather than inferred. Entry and message legality: the record is created by the real handlePreAccept for (Replica 0, Instance 0) at ballot 3 with one PUT command, which is what a recovery-led phase 1 sends to the owner, and the commit is a well-formed single NONE command at ballot 4 with matching replica and instance, which is what the recoverer broadcasts after restarting phase 1 with NOOP; both are protocol messages, so the history is legal for a replica that no longer holds the instance in memory. Oracle and the recover() wrapper: the harness wraps only the delivery in recover so a panic is reported as an event instead of killing the test process; the handler itself is unmodified, and the wrapper is what makes the panic observable rather than what creates it, which the printed panic value confirms. Identity: the prerequisite record event and the commit-result event share instance 0.0, so the observation is tied to the record under test. Inference to termination: the run loop dispatches handlers directly in its select statement with no recover, so a panic in handleCommit propagates out of the loop and ends the process; that step is a source-based inference and is recorded as a limitation rather than as an observed process exit, because the harness does not drive the loop. Contrary evidence and alternatives: the alternative reading that such a record can never belong to the owner is contradicted by the message-created record, and the remaining reservations (dispatcher not modelled, single instance, no history) are recorded as limitations. The item therefore clears correspondence for C4 while keeping the inference boundary explicit.\\\",\n  \\\"limitations\\\":[\\\"the harness observes the panic, not the replica process terminating; the termination step follows from the run loop having no recover and is an inference\\\",\n   \\\"the history that would make a recovery-led PreAccept reach a restarted owner is not constructed; the check fixes the two messages and the record state\\\",\n   \\\"the client-side consequence of the same NOOP recovery is a separate question and is not part of this check\\\"]}]}\njson.dump(sub,open('submission-review-c4.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False)\nprint('ok')\nPY\nID=\"'$(cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -c \"\nimport json;s=json.load(open('\"'state.json'));print([a['id'] for a in s['direct_checks'] if a['id'].startswith('986da6b1')][0])\\\") && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python - \\\"\"'$ID\" <<'\"'PY'\nimport json,sys\ns=json.load(open('submission-review-c4.json'));s['artifact_id']=sys.argv[1]\njson.dump(s,open('submission-review-c4.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False);print(s['artifact_id'])\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run && /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-07_16-54-34-swiftpaxos_epaxos-real-run --submission submission-review-c4.json 2>&1 | head -10\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
